::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-deps, dependencies: list(tomet-address, tomet-ast, tomet-parser, tomet-semantics, tomet-tree), dependents: list(tomet)}

=[tomet-deps]

==[tomet-deps]

Document-level dependency tracking, impact analysis, and incremental invalidation
for Tomet workspaces and static site generators.

==[Architecture & Responsibilities]

- ("Vault-Wide Dependency Graph & Invalidation Engine") `tomet-deps` models document interactions across a vault as a bidirectional directed graph.
It tracks outgoing hypertext links, transclusions/embeds, and metadata dependencies.
- ("Fine-Grained Invalidation") Rather than treating all file modifications equally, `tomet-deps` tracks signature differences:
- Text-only modification: re-renders only the edited document.
- Link addition/removal: re-renders the document and updates the incoming backlinks of the target.
- Title/export changes: propagates re-render requirements to all documents referencing the target.
- Transclusion / Embed: propagates content changes recursively to all embedding documents.

- ("Pure In-Memory & Platform Agnostic") Zero filesystem I/O. All models and graph algorithms are pure in-memory computations,
making `tomet-deps` fully compatible with native CLI, background watch runners, and Wasm targets.

==[Module extract]

Pure in-memory dependency and export extraction from parsed Tomet ASTs.

===[Functions]

====[fn extract_raw_dependencies]

Extracts raw outgoing targets alongside their dependency kind from an AST Document.

====[fn extract_exports_hash]

Computes a hash of document declarations (such as `::meta`, `::title`, `::kind`, `::slug`, etc.).

====[fn extract_document_node]

Builds a [`DocumentNode`] from a parsed document given a target resolution function.

==[Module graph]

In-memory bidirectional dependency graph and impact propagation engine.

===[Structs]

====[struct RemovedRecord]

Record of a document removed from the graph.

====[struct DependencyGraph]

Bidirectional in-memory dependency graph for document nodes.

===[Functions]

====[fn compute_affected_paths]

Pure function: computes affected documents given all document nodes and a slice of changes.

==[Module model]

Pure in-memory data models for document dependencies, backlinks, and invalidation.

===[Structs]

====[struct Dependency]

A directed reference from one document to another.

====[struct Backlink]

An incoming backlink representation.

====[struct DocumentNode]

A document node containing its dependency signature and outgoing references.

====[struct AffectedPaths]

Impact and invalidation report produced by dependency analysis.

===[Enums]

====[enum DependencyKind]

The nature of a directed dependency between two documents.

====[enum Change]

An observed change to a document within a set.

===[Functions]

====[fn fnv1a_hash]

Standard 64-bit FNV-1a hash for content and metadata fingerprinting.
